# GPU plugin: paged attention bounded partials - f16 host sizing plus an
# online-merge partition cap
#
# docs/design-m8-asymmetric-kv.md's follow-up, §7.0.2ab (2026-09-03): on
# the card measured there, the u8:i4 auto-fit lands at 101,984 tokens
# instead of u8's 133,456 because the GENERATE/MIXED-stage mixed attention
# scratch buffer grows with context depth (measured: 932 MiB at 119k
# tokens/chunk 128, the `CL_OUT_OF_RESOURCES` fault §7.0.2ab root-caused to
# the xe driver's rebind worker failing on a full card, "-12" in the
# kernel log). Applied against the pinned runtime, build
# 2026.4.0-22849-71640275d29, on top of patches/0001-0014.
#
# (B) THE RECON CORRECTION, STATED AS A CORRECTION (§7.0.2ab left this
# question open; the source answers it): `tmp_out` is ALREADY f16. Both
# stage-0 and finalization kernels declare it `OUTPUT_TYPE`
# (paged_attention_opt.cl:98, 1037), which `make_layout_jit_constants`
# resolves from the IR's real output dtype - f16 on every model this repo
# serves. Only the HOST sizing was wrong:
# `paged_attention_opt.cpp::get_internal_buffer_descs` hardcoded
# `element_size = 4` and applied it to buffer 7 (tmp_out) unconditionally,
# while buffers 5/6 (exp_sums/max_logits) are correctly 4 B - they are
# genuinely f32 (softmax_accumulator_type). The mixed stage allocated
# exactly twice the bytes its kernels address. Fixed by sizing buffer 7
# with `get_element_size(output_layouts[0].data_type)` instead - no kernel
# line changes, same addresses written and read, half the term. Byte-exact
# by construction; not gated on precision (a 2x over-allocation on u8 was
# not worth preserving as a divergent path).
#
# The f16-range question §7.0.2ab left open is answered by source, not
# inferred: the per-partition softmax divides `slm_qk_vals` by that
# partition's `exp_sum` (paged_attention_opt.cl, pre-patch line 584)
# *before* the V accumulation, so `tmp_out` holds NORMALISED partials - a
# convex combination of dequantised V, O(max|V|) - never an unnormalised
# partial sum. There is no range hazard on this path.
#
# (C) THE ENGINE CONTRACT: one RW config option, wired the way patches/0008
# wired VALUE_CACHE_PRECISION -
#   - `include/intel_gpu/runtime/options.inl`:
#     `OV_CONFIG_RELEASE_OPTION(ov::intel_gpu, paged_attention_max_partitions,
#     0, ...)` - registers the property, generates
#     get_paged_attention_max_partitions()/m_paged_attention_max_partitions
#     the same way every other option in this file does.
#   - `openvino/runtime/intel_gpu/properties.hpp`:
#     `ov::intel_gpu::paged_attention_max_partitions`, string
#     "PAGED_ATTENTION_MAX_PARTITIONS", `Property<size_t, PropertyMutability::RW>`
#     - a genuinely new property (unlike 0008's VALUE_CACHE_PRECISION, no
#     existing public property already covers this).
#   - `plugin.cpp`'s `get_supported_properties()`: added to the RW list next
#     to `moe_cpu_tier_threads`.
#   - `compiled_model.cpp`'s `get_property()`: added to the RO list next to
#     `moe_cpu_tier_threads` (queryable after compile, the way every other
#     property in that list already is).
# 0 (default) is unbounded - every existing caller, byte-identical to
# before this patch existed. The engine detects support by reading the
# property back after compile_model (`core_.get_property(device,
# ov::intel_gpu::paged_attention_max_partitions)`); an unpatched plugin
# throws on the unknown key, and the engine falls back to today's
# depth-scaled reservation term without ever setting the key - the
# fit-term change on the arcint side is out of scope for this task and is
# not part of this patch.
#
# OPERATIONAL NOTE, for the CHANGELOG: this options.inl insertion adds a
# new name to the sorted option set that ov::PluginConfig::visit_attributes
# (de)serializes POSITIONALLY into a GPU model-cache blob - the exact
# mechanism patches/0008's own ExecutionConfig::visit_attributes schema
# guard (execution_config.cpp, "Round 5") exists to catch: a stale-schema
# blob written before this patch fails the guard's signature check and is
# rejected outright (the caller recompiles), not silently misread. That
# guard was built and is expected to do its job here - but the clean,
# quiet way to upgrade to this plugin level is still to clear the GPU
# model cache directory once, exactly as 0008's own header already advises
# for any plugin build that changes this option schema, this one included.
#
# (A) BOUNDED PARTIALS. `seq_len_partition_size` (256) cannot be raised -
# SLM is sized by it and `PAGED_ATTENTION_BLOCKS_PER_PARTITION` derives
# from it, with `SUBGROUP_SIZE == PAGED_ATTENTION_BLOCK_SIZE` enforced by
# `#error`. The bound instead comes from one work-group covering S
# consecutive 256-token partitions:
#
#   - Host (`paged_attention_opt.cpp::update_rt_params`, mirrored in
#     `get_internal_buffer_descs`'s pre-rt_params fallback branch): P = min
#     (raw_partitions, PAGED_ATTENTION_MAX_PARTITIONS) when the option is
#     set and the stage is GENERATE/MIXED (not PREFILL - PREFILL's
#     partition_size is head-size-derived, a different scheme untouched
#     here - and not when has_scores_output() - that path's softmax_
#     results buffer is strided by total_partitions_num but addressed by
#     the fine-grained raw partition index, a separate feature this patch
#     does not rework and would overrun if folded). `rt_params->
#     num_of_partitions` becomes P directly (every exp_sums/tmp_out stride
#     already reads it, so buffer 7's and buffers 5/6's element counts
#     shrink for free); a new `rt_params->partitions_per_wg` carries
#     S = ceil(raw_partitions / P), default 1.
#   - `partitions_per_wg` reaches both the stage-0 kernel (a new trailing
#     scalar argument - it is NOT a JIT constant: unlike
#     PAGED_ATTENTION_MAX_PARTITIONS, which is fixed for a compiled
#     model's lifetime, S varies with context length exactly the way
#     num_of_partitions already does) and both finalization kernels (a
#     second scalar, alongside the pre-existing total_partitions_num).
#   - Kernel, stage 0 (paged_attention_opt.cl): the query load is hoisted
#     above a new `for (uint p = 0; p < partitions_per_wg; ++p)` loop (it
#     does not depend on partition_idx); `wg_partition_idx =
#     get_group_id(2)` is the coarse (0..P-1) index that now addresses
#     exp_sums/max_logits/tmp_out, while the loop's own `partition_idx =
#     wg_partition_idx * partitions_per_wg + p` keeps its original,
#     fine-grained meaning for K/V block addressing. The pre-loop early
#     `return` (unchanged, for wg_partition_idx's own first partition)
#     becomes a `break` inside the loop for a later p that runs out of
#     data - the design's own account of this hazard, and the reason the
#     write is deferred to after the loop rather than done per iteration.
#   - Online merge, folded into the SAME normalisation step that already
#     divides `slm_qk_vals` by `exp_sum` (paged_attention_opt.cl, pre-patch
#     line 584): per q_idx, `m' = max(m, qk_max_p)`, `alpha = s *
#     exp(m - m')`, `beta = exp_sum_p * exp(qk_max_p - m')`; the running V
#     accumulator (`acc` / `acc_lo`+`acc_hi`) is scaled by `alpha /
#     (alpha + beta)` and the normalisation divide is replaced by a
#     multiply by `beta / ((alpha + beta) * exp_sum_p)`; `s = alpha + beta`,
#     `m = m'`.
#   - BIT-EXACTNESS AT PAGED_ATTENTION_MAX_PARTITIONS == 0, BY
#     CONSTRUCTION, NOT BY ALGEBRAIC REDUCTION: partitions_per_wg == 1
#     makes the loop always take p == 0, and p == 0 is a runtime branch
#     to the ORIGINAL, unmerged arithmetic (a straight divide by exp_sum,
#     no accumulator scaling) rather than the general merge formula
#     evaluated at its algebraic identity. This distinction is load-
#     bearing: IEEE 754 division and a multiply by a separately-computed
#     reciprocal-like factor do not round identically even where they are
#     algebraically equal, so the general formula's p == 0 case, however
#     it simplifies on paper, would NOT reproduce the pre-patch kernel bit
#     for bit. acc_scale is declared at loop-body scope (not inside the
#     softmax block where it is computed) because the QK*V block that
#     reads it is a sibling scope, not a child - an ocloc build (below)
#     caught this as an "undeclared identifier" on the first pass, fixed
#     by hoisting the declaration rather than by widening scope
#     informally.
#   - Finalization (both kernels): `num_of_partitions =
#     min(ceil(ceil(effective_seq_len / SEQ_LEN_PARTITION_SIZE) /
#     partitions_per_wg), total_partitions_num)`, replacing the pre-patch
#     `min(ceil(effective_seq_len / SEQ_LEN_PARTITION_SIZE),
#     total_partitions_num)`. partitions_per_wg == 1 makes this identical
#     to the pre-patch formula (integer ceiling division has no rounding-
#     mode ambiguity, unlike the stage-0 merge above) - no runtime branch
#     needed here for the default-off case.
#   - THE HAZARD THE DESIGN NAMES, closed: stage 0's "write tmp_out or
#     write output" predicate and the finalization's num_of_partitions
#     must agree on how many (coarse) partitions a given sequence needs,
#     or a short sequence sharing a mixed-batch dispatch with a longer one
#     can have total_partitions_num > 1 globally while needing only ONE
#     work-group itself, writes tmp_out under the old effective_seq_len >
#     SEQ_LEN_PARTITION_SIZE check, and the finalization's own <= 1 early
#     return never produces `output`. Both sides now compute the same
#     bounded quantity - `seq_bounded_partitions` in stage 0, the
#     restated `num_of_partitions` in the finalization - from the same
#     formula.
#
# PAGED_ATTENTION_MAX_PARTITIONS = 32 and the occupancy/register-pressure
# reasoning behind it are the design's, not verified on this task (no GPU
# device was touched at any point, on P_MAX > 0 OR P_MAX == 0 - nothing in
# this patch, at any bound, has been exercised against the real model).
# Byte-exactness ACROSS this patch's bounded arm is NOT expected and NOT
# claimed - the merge order changes (S partitions merged online per
# work-group, P merged in the finalization, instead of every raw partition
# merged in the finalization), one rounding is folded into the
# normalisation multiply, and (per the review below) up to
# partitions_per_wg - 1 further f16 roundings of the running V accumulator
# itself happen along the merge chain; within an arm the existing ladder
# (cold vs warm, one lane vs two, paged vs stateful) is unaffected by this
# patch and must still hold byte-exact. This "byte-identical when
# unbounded" claim is per-DISPATCH (PAGED_ATTENTION_MAX_PARTITIONS == 0,
# or every sequence in the batch individually needing only 1 partition),
# not per-sequence: partitions_per_wg (S) is computed once per dispatch
# from the batch's OWN longest sequence (update_rt_params reads
# max_context_len across the whole primitive instance), so a short
# sequence sharing a MIXED-stage dispatch with a much longer one that
# triggers folding is folded too, by the same S, even though its own raw
# partition count alone would not have crossed P_MAX - correct (both
# sequences' outputs still merge to the true softmax within tolerance),
# not bit-identical to running that short sequence alone or unbounded.
#
# WHAT THIS PATCH DOES NOT COVER: has_scores_output() sequences (excluded
# from bounding entirely, see above); PREFILL-stage partitioning (a
# different scheme); native 4-bit values in micro-SDPA (backlog, per
# §7.0.2ab); the arcint-side fit-term change in fit.h/backend_ov.cpp that
# would let the engine actually charge 2 bytes and detect this option (out
# of scope for this task, which is the plugin side only); CHANGELOG.md and
# contrib/packaging/marfrit-openvino updates - see the report for why
# those were left alone rather than guessed at.
#
# REVIEW ROUND (Opus, against the post-patch sources, no GPU): found one
# real bug and several documentation/precision gaps, all closed here.
#
#   (1) THE BLOCKER, CONFIRMED BY TRACING THE MATH, NOT JUST TRUSTING THE
#   REVIEW: with SG_SCALE_FACTOR > 1 (get_pa_sg_number_scale_factor returns
#   2 exactly when the KV cache is compressed - u8, u8:i4, the
#   configurations this patch exists for, at 128/256-wide heads), the
#   cross-subgroup reduction that folds the upper half's V-accumulator into
#   the lower half's ran INSIDE the p loop once per iteration but never
#   cleared the upper half's own copy, while the (this patch's own) acc-
#   scale-by-acc_scale step applied unconditionally to both halves by sgid.
#   Consequence, worked through explicitly: at iteration p's end, lower's
#   acc correctly holds the full running total (previous total, scaled,
#   plus this iteration's true partition sum); upper's acc still holds
#   iteration p's own partial (already folded into lower). At iteration
#   p+1's start, BOTH halves get scaled by acc_scale - lower correctly
#   (it is the running total), but upper's now-scaled, already-consumed
#   partial then gets ADDED to lower again by the same reduction at
#   iteration p+1's end. Every folded partition after the first
#   double-counts (and, from p+2 onward, triple- and quadruple-counts) the
#   upper half's own share, compounding with each iteration. Fixed: the
#   upper half resets to zero every iteration instead of scaling (harmless
#   at p == 0, where it already holds zero); this is now also where the
#   rescale multiply moved to SOFTMAX_ACCUMULATOR_TYPE precision (below).
#   Not caught by this task's own first-round test
#   (patches_0015_paged_attention_bounded_partials) because it sets
#   kv_cache_compression = false, which makes SG_SCALE_FACTOR == 1
#   unconditionally (paged_attention_opt.cpp:55-63) - the bug was
#   unreachable by construction, not merely unobserved. Four new cases
#   (patches_0015_paged_attention_sg_scale_2) close that gap: compressed
#   u8:i4 (the blocker case itself) at P_MAX=2 with a 2000-token past,
#   symmetric u4/dual-nibble V at the same bound, the GENERATE
#   (pure-decode, SingleToken dispatch) stage rather than MIXED, and
#   P_MAX=1 (every raw partition folds into the single work-group launched,
#   bypassing the finalization kernel's cross-work-group merge entirely).
#
#   (2) Precision: the rescale multiply now computes in
#   SOFTMAX_ACCUMULATOR_TYPE (float) and stores the result into acc's own
#   OUTPUT_TYPE (f16) - one rounding per iteration, same as before -
#   instead of first casting acc_scale down to f16 and multiplying in f16
#   (two roundings per iteration: the cast, then the product). Does not
#   make the bounded arm byte-exact - up to partitions_per_wg - 1 f16
#   roundings of the accumulator remain along the merge chain at deep
#   contexts (e.g. 14 at 119k tokens, P_MAX=32) - named here explicitly as
#   a tolerance source for the cross-arm comparison in the design's
#   measurement plan, not eliminated. Given a number, on review: f16's
#   unit roundoff is 2^-11 (11 bits of precision, 1 implicit + 10
#   explicit mantissa bits); acc is a convex combination at every step
#   (the merge weights alpha/(alpha+beta) and beta/(alpha+beta) sum to 1),
#   so each of the up-to-(partitions_per_wg - 1) roundings contributes at
#   most one unit-roundoff-sized relative error to the result. At S=15
#   (119k tokens, P_MAX=32), that is <=14 roundings: worst-case bound (the
#   roundings all pushing the same direction, additive) ~= 14 * 2^-11 ~=
#   0.7%; treating them as independent, zero-mean rounding errors instead
#   (the more realistic case) gives an RMS estimate ~= sqrt(14) * 2^-11 ~=
#   0.1%. Use 0.7% as the cross-arm tolerance where a hard bound is
#   needed, 0.1% as the expected typical deviation.
#
#   (3) get_element_size(ov::element::dynamic) returns 0, not a thrown
#   error; a still-unresolved output type at buffer-7 sizing time would
#   have silently allocated a 0-byte buffer instead of failing loud.
#   Asserted non-zero in get_internal_buffer_descs (this task did not
#   observe the output type unresolved at that point - shape can stay
#   dynamic, the element type is not expected to - so this is a defensive
#   assert on an invariant, not a fix for an observed failure). The
#   PREFILL-stage dummy buffer (unused, see above) is now commented as
#   halved relative to before this patch, for the same reason buffer 7
#   itself is - harmless, since PREFILL never addresses it.
#
#   (4) The exp_sums/max_logits write predicate now uses the same
#   seq_bounded_partitions (derived from effective_seq_len, SWA-adjusted)
#   as the tmp_out/output predicate. Before this patch the two predicates
#   already used DIFFERENT quantities under SWA (exp_sums on raw seq_len,
#   tmp_out/output on effective_seq_len) - this patch's unification is a
#   deliberate correction (the two gates must agree or the finalization can
#   read one buffer written and the other not), stated here rather than
#   left implicit, and can only change behaviour for SWA sequences whose
#   full length crosses a partition boundary that their trimmed length does
#   not - exactly the sequences where the two gates already disagreed.
#
