# The fix from the original review round is KEPT in this patch - not
# because it is confirmed, but because it is not DISCONFIRMED either, and
# it remains independently justifiable on structural grounds alone,
# GPU-result-free: the upper SG_SCALE_FACTOR half's accumulator register is
# left holding a value after each iteration's reduction that nothing
# downstream ever reads again except a later iteration's own scale step -
# resetting it to zero is what a value with no further reader should get,
# regardless of whether any specific test's data makes the un-reset path's
# error large enough to matter. Whoever next reads the diagnostic
# assertion's own pass/fail and the sabotage build's result should update
# this section with THAT specific finding, rather than inferring it from
